<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Aragon</h1><p class="st-meta">802 CE – 1035 CE (approx.) · capital Jaca</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The small Pyrenean county around Jaca that gave its name to the Kingdom and later the Crown of Aragon.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The county arose in the early 9th century in the upper valley of the river Aragón, around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaca">Jaca</a>, as a Frankish-backed frontier lordship. Its first known count, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aznar-galindez-i">Aznar Galíndez I</a>, ruled in the 800s under Carolingian protection before being expelled by rivals allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamplona">Pamplona</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Aragon was a mountain county of herders and small farmers, protected by castles and monasteries such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monastery-of-san-juan-de-la-pena">San Juan de la Peña</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monastery-of-san-pedro-de-siresa">San Pedro de Siresa</a>. Its native counts of the Galindo family kept close ties with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamplona">Pamplona</a>, and in the early 10th century the heiress <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andregoto-galindez">Andregoto Galíndez</a> married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garcia-sanchez-i-of-pamplona">García Sánchez I of Pamplona</a>, bringing the county under the Navarrese crown.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Aragon was ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamplona">Pamplona</a> until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sancho-iii-of-navarre">Sancho III</a> died in 1035 and left it to his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramiro-i-of-aragon">Ramiro I</a>, who governed it as a separate realm, the beginning of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-aragon">Kingdom of Aragon</a>, which later grew into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/crown-of-aragon">Crown of Aragon</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/county-of-aragon.jpg" alt="County of Aragon" width="320" height="121"><figcaption>Image: Miguillen · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reino_de_Pamplona_Sancho_III.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>802 CE – 1035 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Jaca</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Aznar Galíndez I, Galindo Aznárez II, Andregoto Galíndez</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Condado de Aragón</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=918&amp;focus=county-of-aragon" aria-label="County of Aragon on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4667 665 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where County of Aragon lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4987 921L5139 672M4987 921L4960 913M4987 921L4979 949"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5139 672h0M4960 913h0M4979 949h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4987 921h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4987 921h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Jaca. <a href="/atlas?year=918&amp;focus=county-of-aragon">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
